{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>הינהק</b> — It has no parallel in biblical language, and it is compared to the language of Kedar." "<b>בלילו</b> — From: \"ויבל לחמורים\" (Genesis 42:27), בליל חמיץ (Exodus 12:34). And the meaning: for one who sits in tranquility does not roar and does not worry, and likewise Job says to his friends, and moreover you speak things that have no substance, and this is the meaning: \"היאכל תפל מבלי מלח\" (Job 6:6)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:54.879277867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}